%N A330442 The number of free polyominoes with n cells which, when drawn on a 2D square grid, contain an Eulerian path.
%C A330442 a(n) is the total number of free polyominoes containing n cells which, when drawn on a 2D square grid, contain an Eulerian path. Such polyominoes must have all edges of length one, see A245620, have one or two edges of length two with all other edges of length one, or else have one edge of length three with all other edges of length one. These edges also include those bordering internal holes.
%C A330442 From _Anthony Detterer_, Sep 05 2026: (Start)
%C A330442 In the drawing of a polyomino on grid paper (every cell edge, with shared edges drawn once), a lattice point has odd degree if and only if exactly two of the four cells surrounding it are present and those two cells share an edge. The drawing is connected, so it has an Eulerian path if and only if the number of such points is 0 or 2. This is a finite check on the four cells around a point, so it is a proof rather than an empirical observation.
%C A330442 a(n) - A245620(n) is the number of these polyominoes whose drawing has exactly two odd-degree vertices, so that the tracing must start and finish at different points. A245620 counts the remainder, where the drawing closes into a single circuit. (End)
